<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="KR2o0025-en-cf52ecef" type="transl"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Translation of 文史通義 into (English)</title><editor role="translator">AI - Gemini</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="2"><ab>This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</ab></availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title/>2026</bibl><ab>Translation of <bibl corresp="#KR2o0025"><title xml:lang="och">文史通義</title></bibl> into <lang xml:lang="en">English</lang>.</ab></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#CH">Initially created: <date>2026-01-30T19:55:26.524+09:00</date> by CH</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Translated parts</head><p xml:id="KR2o0025-start"><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_018-1a.111" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">This, too, by seeking in the manner of the Sū (蘇) family,</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_018-1a.112" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">is mistakenly taken for scholarship.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_018-1a.113" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">This can be observed as an example.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_018-1a.114" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">Someone asked:</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_018-1a.115" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">"According to what you've said,</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_018-1a.116" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">are Hán (韓) and Sū (蘇) not worthy of emulation?" I replied:</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_018-1a.117" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">"Hán (韓) and Sū (蘇) employed their effort and skill</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_018-1a.118" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">merely as an aid to their literary composition.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_018-1a.119" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">They did not consider this (kind of pursuit) to be scholarship."</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-h.1" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">[On Broadness and Conciseness]</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.1" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">Someone asked:</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.2" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">"The imperial examinations are the means by which one discerns a person's scholarship.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.3" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">For the examinations to be fundamentally different from scholarship</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.4" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">is merely a mistake of later degenerate trends.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.5" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">If one is prepared in order to await the examinations,</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.6" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">that is precisely what the *Lǐjì* (禮記) calls 'extensive learning and strong memory in order to await questions.'</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.7" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">How can this not be called scholarship?"</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.8" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">I replied:</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.9" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">"Extensive learning and strong memory</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.10" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">are indeed the affairs of a scholar.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.11" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">However, to consider them the foundation of self-establishment—</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.12" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">that is not where it lies.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.13" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">Learning values being broad yet able to be concise.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.14" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">There has never been anyone who is not broad yet able to be concise.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.15" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">For instance, crude and unrefined scholars</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.16" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">who learn the words of only one teacher and confine themselves to a limited domain,</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.17" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">cannot be called true specialists.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.18" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">But conversely, there has also never been anyone who is not concise yet able to be broad.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.19" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">For instance, common scholars whose memorization is sprawling and confused,</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.20" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">reaching the point of limitlessness,</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.21" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">and vainly seeking to encompass all things,</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.22" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">do not realize that even the wisdom of Yáo (堯) and Shùn (舜) could not achieve this.</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.23" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">Extensive learning and strong memory</seg><seg corresp="#KR2o0025_tls_019-1a.24" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-01-30T19:56:13.921+09:00">can only serve to await questions, that is all."</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>